  annotation "note_1771575113128_4", anchor: "the distinction may matter less than I would prefer", text: "I wrote that sentence knowing it would outlast my professional credibility. The Recitation describes a figure who listened at sealed places and understood before those with power would admit it. The deep ice contains impressions from before penguin civilization — I noted this at the Veil Vents and declined to elaborate. The theological reading and the historical reading converge at the same point: someone has always been listening, and the sealed places have always been imperfect. Whether Hollows is that figure or merely the latest in a tradition of being right too early does not change what he heard. It changes only whether we were warned once or always.", type: :commentary, display: :full
